    "section": "Annex A (Climatic Data)",
    "page": 291,
    "text": "The factor Kd , conductor diameter, is given in 6.4.4.1 as well as the factor Kh , height z above ground. They can be approximated by the following formulae. For in-cloud icing Kd ~ 0,15 d/30 + 0,85 (A.52) NOTE The variation of in-cloud icing with height is very dependent on local topographical and climate conditions. Thus a specific climatological study is suggested to assess this variation for a line exposed to in-cloud icing. and for precipitation icing Kd ~ 0,35 d/30 + 0,65 (A.53) Kh = 0,075 × z / 10 + 0,925 (A.54) The above value of K h for precipitation icing has been obtained using a simple icing model with a wind speed of about 25 km/h at 10 m and droplets fall speed of about 5 m/s.",
